comment_text:
@familyportsmouth
Jesus(God) chose to be born into sinful flesh, although Jesus(God) never sinned while on earth, HE did bare the sins of the entire world 🌎 and of all ages! Which is what ultimately killed Him. 

HE was resurrected by His own power!

@teresasmith4145this which you say isn’t according to the law and the testimony (Isaiah 8:20)

Luke 23:54-56 clearly states that Jesus died on “the preparation” which is a statement only ever used in scripture for the day prior to the seventh day of the week namely “Friday”.

And the Sabbath according to the commandment spoken of in Luke 23:54-56, begins at evening on Friday and ends evening on Saturday — the Hebrew word “Yom” when accompanied by the number 7 literally means the seventh day from evening to the following evening.

@teshafaulkner2270 Were you aware that the Bible endorses slavery? And excludes women from participating in the church?
Ephesians 6:5-8  “Slaves, be obedient to your human masters with fear and trembling, in sincerity of heart, as to Christ”
1 Timothy 2:12, ” I do not permit a woman to teach or to exercise authority over a man; rather, she is to remain quiet.”

@teresasmith4145 Jesus clearly says that he did not come for anyone but for the children of the House of Israel!
Matthew 15:24 
24 But he answered and said, I am not sent but unto the lost sheep of the house of Israel.
